---
<Base title="How Albena works: local-first AI with approvals" description="Albena's architecture: local models on hardware you own, cloud only when needed and allowed, an approval gate for every change, and memory you can erase.">
  <header class="intro">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h1 class="h-display">Personal AI you run yourself.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Albena runs on your own hardware with local models. She is shaped around you, your household or your business, connects to the systems you already use, and never makes a change without your approval.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap chapters">
    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="c1">
      <div class="side"><span class="no">1</span><h2 id="c1">Local first</h2><p>Everyday requests are handled on hardware you own, using local models and Apple on-device intelligence. That keeps them fast and private, and they keep working when the internet does not.</p>
        <ul class="facts"><li>Choose a fast or deep lane per task</li><li>Cloud model only when a task needs it and you allow it</li><li>You are told what leaves your home</li></ul></div>
      <figure class="fig">
        <Diagram id="arch-w" variant="wide" w={900} h={510} nodes={archWide.nodes} edges={archWide.edges} label="Architecture overview" desc="Your voice, screens and devices connect to Albena running on hardware you own. Inside, a lane router chooses local models, which use memory you control. Every request passes an approval gate before reaching your connected systems such as smart home, work tools and cloud services. An optional cloud model is used only if the task needs it and you allow it." />
        <Diagram id="arch-n" variant="narrow" w={360} h={580} nodes={archNarrow.nodes} edges={archNarrow.edges} label="Architecture overview" desc="You talk to Albena. On hardware you own, a lane router picks local models and uses your memory, then an approval gate decides what may reach your systems. An optional cloud model is used only if allowed." />
        <figcaption>Every request passes through the same path. The dashed box is optional and off unless you allow it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="c2">
      <div class="side"><span class="no">2</span><h2 id="c2">You approve every change</h2><p>Reading is instant: ask about anything connected. Anything that changes something is proposed to you first, shown exactly as it will run.</p>
        <ul class="facts"><li>High-risk actions need a change record and your PIN</li><li>Full audit log of what was asked and done</li><li>Rollback information saved with each change</li><li>Per-user permission tiers for the household or team</li></ul></div>
      <figure class="fig">
        <Diagram id="appr-w" variant="wide" w={900} h={400} nodes={apprWide.nodes} edges={apprWide.edges} label="Approval flow" desc="A request is planned. If it only reads, it is answered instantly. If it changes something, it is proposed to you, you approve or decline, then it runs once and is recorded in the audit log with rollback information. High-risk changes also require a change record and your PIN." />
        <Diagram id="appr-n" variant="narrow" w={360} h={500} nodes={apprNarrow.nodes} edges={apprNarrow.edges} label="Approval flow" desc="A request is planned. Reads are answered instantly. Changes are proposed to you, approved or declined, run once, and are logged with rollback information. High-risk changes also need a change record and PIN." />
        <figcaption>Reads are instant. Changes always go through you.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="c3">
      <div class="side"><span class="no">3</span><h2 id="c3">Memory you control</h2><p>Albena keeps her own memory of your people, routines and preferences so you do not repeat yourself. It lives on your hardware first, and you can see and delete any of it.</p>
        <ul class="facts"><li>Learns from usage overnight and proposes improvements</li><li>You approve; she never deploys changes to herself</li><li>Delete one memory or all of them, any time</li></ul></div>
      <figure class="fig">
        <Diagram id="mem-w" variant="wide" w={900} h={340} nodes={memWide.nodes} edges={memWide.edges} label="Memory and learning" desc="Everyday use feeds a nightly review, which creates proposals. You approve them. Memory about people, routines and preferences is kept on your hardware and you can view, edit and delete it at any time." />
        <Diagram id="mem-n" variant="narrow" w={360} h={620} nodes={memNarrow.nodes} edges={memNarrow.edges} label="Memory and learning" desc="Everyday use feeds a nightly review which creates proposals you approve. Memory of people, routines and preferences stays on your hardware, and you can view, edit and delete it." />
        <figcaption>Learning is a proposal, never an automatic change.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="tail">
    <div class="wrap tail-in">
      <p>Want the evidence behind these claims? Read the <a href="/trust">trust center</a> and the <a href="/trust/controls">control mapping</a>. Ready to try it?</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <RelatedLinks keys={['features', 'connectors', 'hardware', 'trust', 'faq']} />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding: 72px 0 40px; background: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 80% at 50% -10%, rgba(113, 112, 255, 0.2), transparent 70%); text-align: center; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 8vw, 72px); max-width: 16ch; margin: 0 auto 20px; }
  .lead { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .chapters { padding-bottom: 40px; }
  .chapter { display: grid; gap: 28px; padding: 56px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .chapter:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .no { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--line-2); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .side h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 34px); letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 560; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .side > p { color: var(--mut); font-size: 16px; }
  .facts { margin-top: 20px; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .facts li { position: relative; padding-left: 22px; color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 14.5px; }
  .facts li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 8px; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--acc); box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--acc); }
  .fig { padding: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; background: var(--panel); min-width: 0; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 12px; text-align: center; font-size: 13px; color: var(--mut); }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) { .chapter { grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; gap: 56px; align-items: start; } .side { position: sticky; top: 88px; } }
  .tail { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 56px 0 72px; }
  .tail-in { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; }
  .tail p { color: var(--mut); max-width: 56ch; }
  .tail a:not(.btn) { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
